# 1. WBS for “Search Restaurants” Feature – Zomato-like App

I selected the **Search Restaurants** feature. A simple Work Breakdown Structure for testing it would look like this:

| WBS No.  | Testing Activity / Sub-task | What will be done?                                                                      |
| -------- | --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **1.0**  | Requirement Study           | Understand how restaurant search is supposed to work.                                   |
| **1.1**  | Test Scenario Preparation   | Identify different search scenarios such as valid, invalid, blank and partial searches. |
| **1.2**  | Test Case Design            | Write detailed test cases with test data and expected results.                          |
| **1.3**  | Test Data Preparation       | Prepare restaurant names, cuisines, keywords and invalid search terms.                  |
| **1.4**  | Test Environment Setup      | Prepare the app, devices, internet connection and required test accounts.               |
| **1.5**  | Functional Testing          | Check whether search gives the correct restaurants and filters.                         |
| **1.6**  | UI/Usability Testing        | Check search box, filters, buttons and results display.                                 |
| **1.7**  | Performance Testing         | Check how quickly search results appear.                                                |
| **1.8**  | Defect Reporting            | Report any incorrect results, crashes or UI issues.                                     |
| **1.9**  | Retesting & Regression      | Retest fixed bugs and make sure existing search functions still work.                   |
| **1.10** | Test Closure                | Prepare the final test result and close the testing activity.                           |

This WBS divides one large testing task into smaller activities, so it becomes easier to assign work and track progress.

