# 3. Estimation Sheet – Flipkart “Apply Coupon” Feature

Since Apply Coupon is a relatively small module, I would keep the estimate smaller.

| Test Activity             | Estimated Hours | Assumption                                                       |
| ------------------------- | --------------: | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Requirement analysis      |             1.5 | Requirements are already available and understandable.           |
| Test scenario creation    |             1.5 | Basic coupon scenarios are covered.                              |
| Test case preparation     |               3 | Around 15–20 test cases are expected.                            |
| Test data preparation     |             1.5 | Valid, expired, invalid and minimum-order coupons are available. |
| Environment setup         |               1 | Existing test environment can be reused.                         |
| Functional test execution |               4 | Testing is mainly manual.                                        |
| Integration testing       |               2 | Coupon system interacts with cart/order calculation.             |
| Defect reporting          |               1 | Assumes only a few defects are found.                            |
| Retesting                 |               2 | Fixes will be available during the testing period.               |
| Regression testing        |               2 | Check cart total and checkout after coupon changes.              |
| Final report              |               1 | Basic test summary is required.                                  |
| **Total**                 |  **20.5 hours** |                                                                  |

### Assumptions

* The coupon feature has already been developed and is available for testing.
* The test environment and test accounts are ready.
* No major changes to requirements are expected.
* The third-party coupon service, if any, is available during testing.
* The estimate is for one tester.

**Estimated effort = 20.5 person-hours.**

